{
  "id": "compressed_air_pipe_line_capacity",
  "title": "Compressed Air Pipe Line Capacity",
  "description": "Capacities of compressed air pipelines - pressure ranging 5 - 250 psi (0.5 - 17 bar). Estimate the flow capacity in a compressed air pipeline based on pipe size and applied pressure.",
  "type": "chart",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Compressed Air Pipe Line Capacity\n\nThis tool estimates the flow capacity in compressed air pipelines with pressure ranging **5 - 250 psi (0.5 - 17 bar)**.\n\n### Assumptions:\n- Schedule 40 pipe\n- For pipes 1/8\" to 1/2\": pressure drop 10% per 100 feet\n- For pipes 3/4\" to 3\": pressure drop 5% per 100 feet\n- Flow measured in SCFM (Standard Cubic Feet per Minute)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "pipe_size",
          "label": "Pipe Size",
          "type": "select",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "1/8\"",
              "value": 0.125
            },
            {
              "label": "1/4\"",
              "value": 0.25
            },
            {
              "label": "3/8\"",
              "value": 0.375
            },
            {
              "label": "1/2\"",
              "value": 0.5
            },
            {
              "label": "3/4\"",
              "value": 0.75
            },
            {
              "label": "1\"",
              "value": 1
            },
            {
              "label": "1.25\"",
              "value": 1.25
            },
            {
              "label": "1.5\"",
              "value": 1.5
            },
            {
              "label": "2\"",
              "value": 2
            },
            {
              "label": "3\"",
              "value": 3
            }
          ],
          "defaultValue": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "applied_pressure_psi",
          "label": "Applied Pressure",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "psi",
          "defaultValue": 100
        },
        {
          "id": "pipe_length",
          "label": "Pipe Length",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "feet",
          "defaultValue": 100
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "capacity_scfm",
          "label": "Flow Capacity",
          "unit": "SCFM",
          "format": "decimal",
          "formula": "inputs.applied_pressure_psi > 0 ? inputs.applied_pressure_psi * 10 : 0"
        },
        {
          "id": "pressure_drop_percent",
          "label": "Pressure Drop",
          "unit": "%",
          "format": "decimal",
          "formula": "inputs.pipe_size <= 0.5 ? 10 : 5"
        },
        {
          "id": "pressure_drop_psi",
          "label": "Pressure Drop",
          "unit": "psi",
          "format": "decimal",
          "formula": "(inputs.pipe_size <= 0.5 ? 10 : 5) * inputs.applied_pressure_psi / 100 * (inputs.pipe_length / 100)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chart",
      "options": {
        "title": {
          "text": "Compressed Air Pipeline Capacity vs Pressure",
          "left": "center"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "trigger": "axis"
        },
        "xAxis": {
          "type": "category",
          "data": [
            "5 psi\n(0.3 bar)",
            "20 psi\n(1.4 bar)",
            "40 psi\n(2.8 bar)",
            "60 psi\n(4.1 bar)",
            "80 psi\n(5.5 bar)",
            "100 psi\n(6.9 bar)",
            "150 psi\n(10.3 bar)",
            "200 psi\n(13.8 bar)",
            "250 psi\n(17.2 bar)"
          ]
        },
        "yAxis": {
          "type": "value",
          "name": "Flow Capacity (SCFM)"
        },
        "series": [
          {
            "name": "1/2\" Pipe",
            "data": [
              15,
              35,
              65,
              95,
              125,
              150,
              220,
              280,
              330
            ],
            "type": "line",
            "smooth": true
          },
          {
